We need to stop "making RIG look like SCRIPT" and instead make RIG USE THE
SAME 3D WORKSPACE PATTERN as SCRIPT.

The current RIG is still architecturally separate:

    <RigViewport size={420} ... />

inside a centred box, with its own:

- renderer
- PerspectiveCamera
- orbit maths
- wheel zoom
- grid
- lights
- fixed sizing
- camera behaviour

That is why it never quite matches SCRIPT.

USER REQUIREMENT:

    FORGE -> RIG

must have the EXACT SAME 3D WORLD SPACE and RIGHT-BAR EXPERIENCE as SCRIPT.

Not "similar".
Not "same colours".
Not another manually matched renderer.

Use the existing SCRIPT world behaviour as the reference implementation.

